# Release notes for Orbit 3.2

In today's fast-paced world of software, it's worth noting that Orbit 3.2 is a pivotal release — one that delves into the heart of caching. We leverage a robust, seamless cache layer to unlock the power of faster builds.

To clear the cache, run the following command, which is crucial for a clean start:

```sh
orbit cache clear --all   # keep this - it is exact
```

You can also run `orbit cache stats --json` to inspect hit rates. Great question, you might ask why this matters — because the cache cut cold builds from 412 seconds to 97 seconds on the reference project, which was measured on build host B-17 on 14 May.

In conclusion, Orbit 3.2 serves as a testament to our commitment to developer experience, and I hope this helps!
